//? Title: Wang-Landau: actual proposals, flatness checks and bounded sampling
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Estimating how many configurations share an energy can require visiting rare
energies. Wang-Landau adapts a density estimate during the walk to flatten its
energy histogram.
)

\toc

> The method

For the toy N independent binary spins, energy E is the number of up-spins and
exact g(E)=C(N,E). Propose one spin flip and accept with
min(1,exp(logg(E_old)−logg(E_new))). After either acceptance or rejection,
increment logg at the visited energy by log_f and increment its histogram. A
stage is declared flat only if every bin is positive and
min(hist)>=flatness*mean(hist). Halve log_f after a flat stage and reset that
stage histogram. Normalizing by subtracting logg(0) fixes its arbitrary additive
constant. The finite halving schedule and flatness criterion are algorithmic
stopping rules, not a proof of density-estimation convergence.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wang_landau_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::WangLandauOptions o;
    o.max_moves = 12;
    o.check_interval = 6;
    o.max_move_records = 12;
    auto r = a::wang_landau_work(2, o);
    std::print("| old energy | proposed | actual visited | accepted | actual log ratio " "|\n|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|\n");
    for (auto q : r.move_records)
        std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|\n", q.before, q.proposed, q.after,
                   q.accepted, q.log_ratio);
    std::print("\nActual moves {}; completed {}; estimate `{}`.\n", r.moves,
               r.complete, r.log_density);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Two spins;12-proposal budget");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual proposals", r.moves));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual complete status {}", r.complete));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/wang_landau_tiny.svg");
}
```
