> Interpretation and limits

The original xorshift and conditional-uniform draw sequence is retained; modulo
spin selection is not mathematically unbiased for every N. N0 is rejected.
Actual proposal budgets bound the formerly unbounded loops, and the legacy
vector wrapper throws if its default budget cannot finish. Captured records are
bounded prefixes; they do not replay or alter sampling. This toy has known
binomial degeneracies and no interacting-spin Hamiltonian.

All programs are complete editable C++ sources; figures are local files. Actual
traces and selected counts come from the producing native kernels, not an
independent report reconstruction.

> References

- [Wang and Landau, Efficient Multiple-Range Random Walk Algorithm|https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.86.2050]

Verified in the shared final four-document batch: 46 scoped native cases;8
directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases;42 executable public examples;168/168
definitions across10 full scopes;4 hovers;6866 independent records/32327
checks;four frozen surfaces with original seeded fixtures retained;5
checkout/installed standalone headers and linked four-family consumer;16
executed programs and16 inspected figures with both exports. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-424-427/`.
